WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.630
When her grandmother objects
to her going to America,

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.500
Mitsuki decides to leave home
without saying anything.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:09.830
But when she finds out that her grandmother
used to go to a music school,

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.730
she is motivated to
try to persuade her again.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.300
She ended up going
without getting permission,

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:19.400
but I think her feelings
got through to her grandmother.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.060
So, I wonder what's going to
happen today...

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:28.930
Got that?

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:29.900
Yes.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:19.600
In any case, it's hard to believe
your grandmother gave you her permission.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:24.060
On the other hand,
she didn't say anything to us.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.530
<i>Grandma...</i>

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:41.800
<i>Eichi went off to America</i>
<i>like this two years ago too.</i>

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.800
<i>Eichi, I'm coming now.</i>

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.600
Wow!

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:25.700
Wow! I'm really here in America.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:30.060
More importantly, how are we gonna
find her? With this many people...

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.030
Welcome to America!

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:33.560
Ms. Kazumi!

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:39.300
Welcome, Mitsuki!
I'm proud of you for coming all this way!

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:42.100
Anything to see Eichi!

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:44.030
That's right.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:46.760
- No one can get in the way of my dream!
- No one can get in the way of my dream!

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:52.060
Oh, Ms. Kazumi,
let me introduce you.

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:55.360
This is Dr. Wakaoji
and Ms. Oshige.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.500
I'm Wakaoji. Nice to meet you

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:58.930
I'm Oshige.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:03.160
I'm Kazumi Franklin.
Very nice of you to come.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.530
Thank you for having us.
It is an honor to meet you.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:09.760
Of course,
there's no one to greet us.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:11.260
That's the way it goes.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.200
Oh, Takuto!

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:17.300
Don't, Nick!

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:21.000
Oh? So that baby is yours,
Ms. Kazumi?

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:23.960
That's right. This is my son Nick
and my husband Jim.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:28.000
Nice to meet you, Mr. Franklin.

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:30.830
Nice to meet you, Mitsuki.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:31.860
Huh?

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.230
Nevada...you said?

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:43.830
Yes, there's someone in a town
at the edge of Lake Roslyn there

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:46.430
who knows Mr. and Mrs. Sakurai.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:49.660
It's about ten hours
by car from here.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:52.360
What?! It's that far?!

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:55.430
It's that way.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:56.660
Oh, okay.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:01.660
<i>I'm coming to see you, Eichi.</i>

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:05.660
But Ms. Kazumi,
how did you find out?

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:09.000
I have a bit of
an information network.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:09.700
What?!

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:16.200
<i>Is that a shady and mysterious group?</i>
<i>Or perhaps a shady psychic?</i>

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:21.230
I think it'll be all right if you see that person,
but do you want me to go with you?

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:26.430
Knowing that much is the same as
finding him. We'll be all right on our own.

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:27.500
I see.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:31.830
Well, here's that person's address.
If you need anything, please contact me.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:32.730
Yes.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.200
<i>So it's Eichi...</i>

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:41.260
<i>I wonder why I'm starting to</i>
<i>acknowledge Eichi's existence now.</i>

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:46.430
<i>I had no real sense of him</i>
<i>when we were in Japan.</i>

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:54.230
<i>Eichi, I've finally come</i>
<i>all the way here.</i>

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:06.630
We're here!

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.760
Wow, it's beautiful!

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.760
Oh, I'm envious!

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:15.160
What's up with that?

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:19.360
Remember, she's said before, she likes
rooms with a view of the ocean.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:22.200
But it's the same Pacific Ocean.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:26.800
In that sense, I guess Japan
and America are connected.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:28.460
Come to think of it,

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:33.900
Eichi once said that the Pacific Ocean
is exactly the same size as the moon.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:34.600
Huh?

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:37.260
So the moon was once
in the Pacific Ocean?!

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.360
I don't know about that.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:45.060
Maybe the lost Mu continent was the moon?
If so, that's incredible!

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:46.730
There's no chance of that!

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:52.930
<i>Grandma...</i>

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:57.500
<i>Please listen to</i>
<i>my songs someday.</i>

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:37.630
<i>Mitsuki, you can only see</i>
<i>one face of the moon from Earth.</i>

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:46.630
<i>Even such a beautiful moon has marks</i>
<i>on the other side from meteors falling on it.</i>

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:52.400
<i>Continuing to shine</i>
<i>despite the scars.</i>

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:57.400
<i>When I first met you, Mitsuki,</i>
<i>I thought it was a perfect name for you.</i>

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:10.360
Ms. Kazumi...

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:13.530
Mitsuki, do you remember
this photograph?

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:14.330
What?

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:19.830
I-I remember it.

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:25.700
Oh? Mitsuki doesn't look happy
at all in the photograph.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:27.230
I know.

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:29.430
I don't know what happened
at the Christmas party,

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:30.800
but she sulked the whole time.

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:33.730
Did you have a fight
with Eichi or something?

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:36.130
Let me see,
I forget what happened.

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:38.030
Oh, you don't remember?

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:40.830
<i>I remember.</i>

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:45.830
<i>On the night of</i>
<i>the Christmas party.</i>

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.730
<i>Your hands are warm, Eichi.</i>

00:08:58.000 --> 00:08:58.660
<i>Mitsuki...</i>

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:02.930
<i>There'll come a day</i>
<i>when we'll be separated.</i>

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:07.300
<i>That won't happen!</i>
<i>We'll always be together.</i>

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:14.130
<i>Isn't that right?</i>

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:20.830
<i>I don't know. But if and when that happens,</i>
<i>I'm afraid you'll forget me and leave.</i>

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:27.430
<i>That's why I want you to always</i>
<i>let me be near you like this.</i>

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:40.100
<i>Mitsuki...I really like you.</i>

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:50.260
<i>Now everyone,</i>
<i>look at the camera.</i>

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:52.100
<i>- Okay!</i>
<i>- Okay!</i>

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:03.060
<i>Okay, everyone smile!</i>
<i>One, two...</i>

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:13.800
<i>It was after that...when I was told that</i>
<i>Eichi would be going to America.</i>

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:29.600
Oh, Nick!

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:31.460
You shouldn't be so rough!

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:34.930
Please, I'm asking you.

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:37.000
Here, I'll lift you way high up.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.030
Actually...

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:44.600
He was lost...and when I took
him to where he wanted to go,

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:47.600
he asked to take me out
to dinner to thank me.

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:52.700
But I didn't know that you were
fluent in English, Ms. Kazumi.

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:56.530
No, Jim was fluent in Japanese.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:57.760
Oh...

00:10:57.860 --> 00:10:59.330
But I was surprised.

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:03.200
As soon as our meal ended,
he asked me to go out with him.

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:07.260
I couldn't help but ask you.
It was love at first sight.

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:10.600
But of course I couldn't
give my answer right there.

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:11.960
Y-Yeah.

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:16.030
<i>Mitsuki...I really like you.</i>

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:20.900
Of course.

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:25.530
So I later replied with a video letter.

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:26.760
Oh, that was when...

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:29.900
I was happy when I
received the video letter.

00:11:30.230 --> 00:11:32.700
I thought it was
the happiest day of my life.

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:39.730
<i>I didn't even know I'd</i>
<i>soon be apart from Eichi.</i>

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:05.260
<i>I just kept running away...</i>
<i>simply because I was embarrassed.</i>

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:32.260
So you've at least heard of them,
right, Mitsuki?

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:35.400
The musical actress Eleanor Pain

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:38.530
and the vocalist Steel of
the hard rock band THEM.

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:39.460
Yeah.

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:43.360
Apparently their throats were fixed
through Dr. Lon Herberd's surgeries.

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:45.030
Is that so?

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:48.360
Thanks for waiting, you two.

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:51.330
This is Dr. Lon Herberd.

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:52.700
Hello.

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:56.960
What do you think?

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:02.900
I think your measures to stop the progress
with medication were appropriate.

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:05.730
However, surgery will
be needed in due course.

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:09.900
But it may be difficult from a stamina
standpoint given this girl's age.

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:13.600
Her mentality is also
an important element.

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:19.730
The best choice would be for you,
a person she absolutely trusts,

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:24.530
to perform the surgery in your hospital where
there'd be no communication difficulties.

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:25.600
I understand.

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:31.160
If your hospital expresses a reluctance to
bring in the equipment, we could do it here.

00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:32.730
Thank you very much.

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:35.360
- Tony, how does your throat feel?
- I'll do my best to convince them so

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:36.900
- It's all right, Mom.
- the operation can take place in Japan.

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:41.230
The doctor also told me to let
my throat gradually get used to it.

00:13:41.530 --> 00:13:45.160
Really? I'm so glad. At one point,
I didn't know what would happen.

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:47.160
Not that again.

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:51.200
- That child was the same as you,
- You're such a worrier.

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:53.500
but he's recovered to that point.

00:13:54.460 --> 00:13:56.830
I want you to get well like that too.

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:09.960
Herberd... Herberd...
Nothing.

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:15.500
W-Well, it is work.

00:14:15.530 --> 00:14:18.660
What? You don't need
to tell me that. I know.

00:14:18.930 --> 00:14:22.130
Oh... I see.
If that's the case, then...

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:25.900
Looks like they're done.

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:29.500
So, next we have to go make
an appearance at AAS Broadcasting.

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:31.100
I need to transform her.

00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:36.960
I thought he was criticizing me,
but it was only my imagination.

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:40.430
Oh, this is throwing me off.

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:46.660
So now our work is done.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:47.530
Yes.

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:52.730
Meroko!
What's the matter?

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:56.730
Oh, I guess there's
no use worrying.

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:03.830
Come on, let's go sightseeing!
Let's go!

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:05.160
Let's do that!

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:06.300
Yeah!

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:15.030
All right!

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:16.530
Wow!

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:19.730
Watch out!

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:21.930
It's your first time, right?

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:23.230
Yes.

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:25.930
I'll hold your hand.

00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:27.200
Thank you.

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:42.330
- Hi!
- Hi!

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:43.600
- Hi!
- Hi!

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:51.060
Maybe it's the nice weather,
but she looks healthy too.

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:57.800
We Death Spirits really don't fit in
on the West Coast, huh, Meroko?

00:15:59.360 --> 00:16:00.360
Meroko?

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:09.430
So it's only me that doesn't fit in.

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:20.930
There!

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:21.630
There!

00:16:24.360 --> 00:16:25.030
There!

00:16:25.660 --> 00:16:26.760
Go Mitsuki!

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:27.460
There!

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:30.060
I did it!

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:31.100
Yay!

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:44.230
<i>Maybe I shouldn't have</i>
<i>come to America.</i>

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:46.700
<i>She looks like</i>
<i>she's having fun.</i>

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:50.430
<i>That's understandable.</i>
<i>She is closer to Eichi.</i>

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:53.660
<i>So what is it that</i>
<i>I want to do?</i>

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:56.760
<i>She's a human and</i>
<i>I'm a Death Spirit.</i>

00:16:57.300 --> 00:17:00.500
<i>Even if I could share my feelings,</i>
<i>what would happen?</i>

00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:03.830
<i>I can't make her happy.</i>

00:17:05.860 --> 00:17:09.300
<i>More importantly,</i>
<i>she likes Eichi.</i>

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:12.200
<i>There's no need for me.</i>

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:19.330
<i>I fully understand this,</i>
<i>but why can't I tear myself away?</i>

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:31.600
That was fun!

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:33.130
It really was!

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:35.260
Welcome back!

00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:36.760
- We're home!
- We're home!

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:38.500
Oh, New Year's pine decorations?

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:42.000
Tomorrow is New Year's.
So we do this as a Japanese custom.

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:45.830
That's right, let's all eat noodles
to ring in the New Year tonight!

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:47.530
Really?

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:49.460
Here, eat up!

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.500
- Thank you!
- This looks great!

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:54.900
I never thought I'd come
all the way to America

00:17:54.930 --> 00:17:56.960
and be able to eat noodles
to welcome in the New Year.

00:17:57.700 --> 00:18:00.230
Right? Eat as much as you'd like.

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:01.160
Thank you.

00:18:04.030 --> 00:18:07.360
<i>Even when I knew Eichi</i>
<i>was going to America,</i>

00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:10.430
<i>I still couldn't say</i>
<i>anything to him.</i>

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:34.560
<i>So this is where you were.</i>

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:46.730
<i>You don't need to pick it up.</i>

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:47.860
<i>What?!</i>

00:18:52.460 --> 00:18:57.130
<i>Mitsuki, sorry for making you worry.</i>
<i>Please forget about me.</i>

00:18:58.130 --> 00:18:59.330
<i>You don't need to worry anymore.</i>

00:19:01.600 --> 00:19:05.060
<i>Y-You're mistaken! I...</i>
<i>Wait, Eichi!</i>

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:07.700
<i>The pendant!</i>

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:15.560
<i>The same Eichi that said he was afraid</i>
<i>of being forgotten told me to forget him.</i>

00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:20.300
<i>I made such a nice person say</i>
<i>something to push me away.</i>

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:27.760
<i>I realized that I liked Eichi as I cried,</i>
<i>thinking about how much he thought of me.</i>

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:35.160
<i>I found it!</i>

00:19:39.430 --> 00:19:44.060
<i>After that, I was somehow</i>
<i>able to talk to Eichi,</i>

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:48.230
<i>but ultimately, the day to say goodbye came</i>
<i>before I was able to tell him I liked him.</i>

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:51.930
<i>I won't forget any of you.</i>
<i>Take care.</i>

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:57.260
<i>- Bye bye!</i>
<i>- Take care!</i>

00:19:57.300 --> 00:19:59.030
<i>Take care, Eichi!</i>

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:07.460
<i>No! No!</i>
<i>Don't go, Eichi.</i>

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:12.460
<i>Don't cry, Mitsuki.</i>
<i>America isn't that far away.</i>

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:13.900
<i>But...</i>

00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:20.200
<i>So let's make a promise that we'll</i>
<i>be closer to achieving our dreams</i>

00:20:20.230 --> 00:20:21.760
<i>than we are now</i>
<i>when we next meet.</i>

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:24.360
<i>I wanna be an astronomer.</i>

00:20:24.860 --> 00:20:26.160
<i>And you wanna be a singer.</i>

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:38.130
<i>He may have</i>
<i>understood my feelings,</i>

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:41.830
<i>but in the end, I wasn't able</i>
<i>to tell him that liked him.</i>

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:07.860
W-What?
New Year's Eve bells even in America?

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:11.300
No, those are church bells.

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:26.300
<i>But this time I'll say it.</i>

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:30.530
<i>That I really like you, Eichi.</i>

00:23:06.930 --> 00:23:10.230
She's so stupid! Being in America
has made her so careless!

00:23:10.360 --> 00:23:11.930
What's wrong, Takuto?!

00:23:12.560 --> 00:23:15.630
Mitsuki lost the pendant
she's always wearing!

00:23:15.800 --> 00:23:19.830
You mean, the precious pendant
that Eichi gave her?

00:23:20.260 --> 00:23:23.160
Jeez, I can't believe it.
I'm gonna go help her find it.

00:23:23.600 --> 00:23:25.830
Takuto! Wait up!

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:30.800
Next time on Full Moon:
"The Stolen Pendant."

00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:32.430
- Look forward to it!
- Look forward to it!
